def brute(nums):
    MOD=10**9+7
    mx = max(nums)
    bestM = None; bestk=None
    for k in range(2, mx+3):
        # kadane
        best = None; cur = 0
        for x in nums:
            v = x if x % k == 0 else -x
            if best is None:
                cur = v; best = v
            else:
                cur = max(cur + v, v)
                best = max(best, cur)
        if bestM is None or best > bestM:
            bestM = best; bestk = k
    return (bestM % MOD) * (bestk % MOD) % MOD

For k up to mx+2: includes at least one non-divisor (mx+1 and mx+2 both > mx so divide nothing). Good; brute will correctly capture M and smallest achieving k. For all-ones, mx=1, k in 2..3, both give -1, bestk=2, answer -2 mod. Matches.

